cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper."
title: "sincFeyn: Sinc-function evaluation of QED vertex graphs for the electron g-2"
authors:
  - family-names: Easther
    given-names: Richard
    affiliation: "University of Auckland"
license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
repository-code: "https://github.com/reasther/sincFeyn"
abstract: >-
  Two-, three- and four-loop QED contributions to the electron anomalous magnetic moment, and a
  sample of five-loop graphs, from
  Schwinger-parametric integrands with Volkov's pointwise forest subtraction, evaluated by
  pruned hierarchical Sinc (trapezoid in ln s) sums. The code was written almost entirely by an
  AI coding assistant (Claude, Anthropic) under the author's direction.
